1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:07,000
Ichikawa, can you be our student rep and read a farewell address to our graduating class?

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:09,000
Yeah, I don't think so.

3
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:11,000
What? No way, that's awesome!

4
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:15,000
Yeah, maybe, but this is something important that an honor student should probably do.

5
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:18,000
Someone like Ishimura or even Hara.

6
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:19,000
What about me?

7
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:21,000
Be my guest.

8
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:25,000
A farewell speech? Why not you? You've got good grades.

9
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:27,000
Got the second highest grade on our final.

10
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:29,000
Wait, that's amazing! You did?

11
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:34,000
Oh, you didn't hear. I was all happy about doing a little better and then...

12
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:37,000
Well, I got the second best grade.

13
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:39,000
You should do it!

14
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:41,000
Him? Giving a farewell speech?

15
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:42,000
Hilarious!

16
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:44,000
This isn't all about grades though.

17
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:48,000
Okay, okay. I'm not trying to force you here or anything.

18
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:52,000
But we have a rehearsal tomorrow and no one has taken the role yet.

19
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:53,440
Oh, you were all right now.

20
00:00:53,440 --> 00:00:55,440
Uh...

21
00:00:57,000 --> 00:00:57,940
Hmm.

22
00:00:57,940 --> 00:00:59,040
Oh!

23
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:02,500
Uh!

24
00:01:02,500 --> 00:01:04,500
Just until you find someone then!

25
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:06,500
If it's just rehearsal...

26
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:09,000
Then I guess I can do it.

27
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:38,980
Thank you.

28
00:02:42,036 --> 00:02:50,636
Next, a farewell address from our student representative, Kiyotaro Ichikawa.

29
00:02:50,636 --> 00:02:51,636
Huh?

30
00:02:51,636 --> 00:03:00,636
I should have said no.

31
00:03:00,636 --> 00:03:09,516
Farewell graduating students, the day your journey begins has come, despite the harsh

32
00:03:09,516 --> 00:03:14,756
cold, the rays of spring fall warm upon us now, I will show up with you celebrating your

33
00:03:14,756 --> 00:03:15,756
Can't hear a word.

34
00:03:15,756 --> 00:03:18,756
He's just whispering.

35
00:03:18,756 --> 00:03:23,756
Who is that?

36
00:03:23,756 --> 00:03:28,556
He's a nervous wreck.

37
00:03:28,556 --> 00:03:31,076
It sounded to me like you were whispering up there.

38
00:03:31,076 --> 00:03:34,436
That's too bad, trouble with the sound system, I guess.

39
00:03:34,436 --> 00:03:36,676
I died out there.

40
00:03:36,676 --> 00:03:39,916
Nice try.

41
00:03:39,916 --> 00:03:44,356
Whatever, I bet they'll look for someone else now, and find by me.

42
00:03:44,356 --> 00:03:45,916
Let's practice, come on.

43
00:03:45,916 --> 00:03:46,916
Huh?

44
00:03:46,916 --> 00:03:47,916
What?

45
00:03:47,916 --> 00:03:49,916
Come on, I'm not gonna do this.

46
00:03:49,916 --> 00:03:52,916
I take voice lessons and stuff, don't worry.

47
00:03:52,916 --> 00:03:55,916
Now, focus on your diaphragm.

48
00:03:55,916 --> 00:04:01,676
Um, the diaphragm is higher up.

49
00:04:01,676 --> 00:04:10,356
In closing, I hope that you all remain in good health, and accomplish great things.

50
00:04:10,356 --> 00:04:12,356
And from all of us, farewell.

51
00:04:12,356 --> 00:04:13,356
Wow!

52
00:04:13,356 --> 00:04:14,916
That was much better!

53
00:04:14,916 --> 00:04:15,916
Good job!

54
00:04:15,916 --> 00:04:18,916
Standing straight like this is exhausting.

55
00:04:18,916 --> 00:04:20,356
That was great!

56
00:04:20,356 --> 00:04:23,356
Must be because you're second in our grade.

57
00:04:23,356 --> 00:04:26,596
You're the one who gave me voice lessons just now.

58
00:04:26,596 --> 00:04:31,076
Yeah, I know, but...

59
00:04:31,076 --> 00:04:33,236
Why didn't you tell me?

60
00:04:33,236 --> 00:04:36,836
If I was second in our grade, I'd be bragging to everyone.

61
00:04:36,836 --> 00:04:38,516
It's not really that big of a deal.

62
00:04:38,516 --> 00:04:41,476
School grades are nothing more than small steps.

63
00:04:41,476 --> 00:04:44,036
What's important is where you let them lead you.

64
00:04:44,036 --> 00:04:48,716
That's so professional!

65
00:04:48,716 --> 00:04:54,876
So, the other day, you came and saw me at work, yeah?

66
00:04:54,876 --> 00:04:58,476
And cuz of that, you got to see me trying my best.

67
00:04:58,476 --> 00:05:01,596
I wanna see you try.

68
00:05:01,596 --> 00:05:08,756
Psst!

69
00:05:08,756 --> 00:05:10,756
Go out with me, please.

70
00:05:10,756 --> 00:05:18,236
Sorry, I can't.

71
00:05:18,236 --> 00:05:22,396
It's just... there's someone else I really like.

72
00:05:22,396 --> 00:05:24,196
Yamada?

73
00:05:24,196 --> 00:05:26,476
Mm-hmm.

74
00:05:26,476 --> 00:05:28,316
You're better off dating someone else.

75
00:05:28,316 --> 00:05:33,116
Then why do we always go out so much?

76
00:05:33,116 --> 00:05:35,676
I don't wanna see the look on her face.

77
00:05:35,676 --> 00:05:37,676
This guy really meant it.

78
00:05:40,756 --> 00:05:42,396
I'll do it.

79
00:05:42,396 --> 00:05:43,396
Huh?

80
00:05:43,396 --> 00:05:46,236
The address.

81
00:05:46,236 --> 00:05:48,236
It's time to stand proud.

82
00:05:48,236 --> 00:05:50,236
To let her see.

83
00:05:50,236 --> 00:05:52,236
To let him see.

84
00:05:54,236 --> 00:05:56,236
Or so I said.

85
00:05:56,236 --> 00:06:00,236
On behalf of all of us here, I wish you all the best.

86
00:06:00,236 --> 00:06:01,236
Mm... quit staring.

87
00:06:01,236 --> 00:06:04,236
But you asked me to sit here and watch you read your speech.

88
00:06:04,236 --> 00:06:06,876
You said it was the only way it counted as practice.

89
00:06:06,876 --> 00:06:08,716
Uh, sorry.

90
00:06:08,716 --> 00:06:11,716
When did I start getting scared of being in front of people?

91
00:06:11,716 --> 00:06:16,716
The award for best traffic safety poster goes to Kyo-Taro Ichikawa.

92
00:06:16,716 --> 00:06:18,716
Congratulations.

93
00:06:22,716 --> 00:06:25,716
Huh, these ignoramuses, they're nothing compared to me.

94
00:06:25,716 --> 00:06:29,356
I've fallen a long way from my old self.

95
00:06:29,356 --> 00:06:30,356
All right, bro.

96
00:06:30,356 --> 00:06:31,356
I brought the humidifier.

97
00:06:31,356 --> 00:06:33,356
And the third stuff you rub on.

98
00:06:33,356 --> 00:06:34,356
Ah!

99
00:06:34,356 --> 00:06:35,356
Ah!

100
00:06:35,356 --> 00:06:36,356
Okay, rub this on your chest.

101
00:06:36,356 --> 00:06:37,356
What are you doing?

102
00:06:37,356 --> 00:06:39,036
This stuff is for colds.

103
00:06:39,036 --> 00:06:40,036
Whatever.

104
00:06:40,036 --> 00:06:41,836
I just have to read the basic script.

105
00:06:41,836 --> 00:06:43,276
It's no big deal.

106
00:06:43,276 --> 00:06:45,796
What I need, though, is a haircut.

107
00:06:45,796 --> 00:06:48,236
Will 2,000 yen do?

108
00:06:48,236 --> 00:06:49,236
No.

109
00:06:49,236 --> 00:06:51,036
I need more like 5,000.

110
00:06:51,036 --> 00:06:52,036
Huh?

111
00:06:52,036 --> 00:06:53,036
No way!

112
00:06:53,036 --> 00:06:57,036
Are you making your haircut debut?

113
00:06:57,036 --> 00:07:02,276
Great system for antisocial folks.

114
00:07:02,276 --> 00:07:03,976
Okay, then.

115
00:07:03,976 --> 00:07:05,576
What are you writing?

116
00:07:05,576 --> 00:07:08,476
A flow chart for my conversation with the hairstylist.

117
00:07:08,476 --> 00:07:12,256
I need to think up easy ways to tell them what kind of haircut I want, too.

118
00:07:12,256 --> 00:07:15,056
Uh, want me to go with you?

119
00:07:15,056 --> 00:07:17,956
Definitely not.

120
00:07:17,956 --> 00:07:20,536
And so, I readied myself for the hair salon.

121
00:07:20,536 --> 00:07:26,916
But they must have labeled me the non-social type, because we didn't share a word the whole

122
00:07:26,916 --> 00:07:27,916
time.

123
00:07:27,916 --> 00:07:29,916
Take a look.

124
00:07:29,916 --> 00:07:30,916
Thanks.

125
00:07:30,916 --> 00:07:35,916
These fancy places are something else.

126
00:07:35,916 --> 00:07:41,596
And so, I'm Kiyotaro Ichikawa, and I speak for all of us.

127
00:07:41,596 --> 00:07:42,596
Huh?

128
00:07:42,596 --> 00:07:43,596
Quit crying!

129
00:07:43,596 --> 00:07:44,596
Why should I?

130
00:07:44,596 --> 00:07:49,976
And just like that, graduation was here.

131
00:07:49,976 --> 00:07:50,976
Huh?

132
00:07:50,976 --> 00:07:53,976
Why does this look different after just one day?

133
00:07:53,976 --> 00:07:54,976
Huh?

134
00:07:54,976 --> 00:07:55,976
Huh?

135
00:07:55,976 --> 00:07:56,976
Huh?

136
00:07:56,976 --> 00:07:57,976
Huh?

137
00:07:57,976 --> 00:07:58,976
Huh?

138
00:07:58,976 --> 00:07:59,976
Huh?

139
00:07:59,976 --> 00:08:00,976
Huh?

140
00:08:00,976 --> 00:08:01,976
Huh?

141
00:08:01,976 --> 00:08:02,976
Huh?

142
00:08:02,976 --> 00:08:03,976
Huh?

143
00:08:03,976 --> 00:08:04,976
Huh?

144
00:08:04,976 --> 00:08:05,976
Huh?

145
00:08:05,976 --> 00:08:06,976
Huh?

146
00:08:06,976 --> 00:08:07,976
Huh?

147
00:08:07,976 --> 00:08:08,976
Wow!

148
00:08:08,976 --> 00:08:09,976
Your hair's real short!

149
00:08:09,976 --> 00:08:10,976
You look rich!

150
00:08:10,976 --> 00:08:11,976
What happened?

151
00:08:11,976 --> 00:08:12,976
Uh, nothing.

152
00:08:12,976 --> 00:08:14,976
Just went to a new place, and it came out weird is all.

153
00:08:14,976 --> 00:08:17,976
Make it sound like it wasn't the first time you ever went.

154
00:08:17,976 --> 00:08:19,976
You use any wax?

155
00:08:19,976 --> 00:08:20,976
Hm?

156
00:08:20,976 --> 00:08:21,976
What wax?

157
00:08:21,976 --> 00:08:22,976
Wait.

158
00:08:22,976 --> 00:08:23,976
Hang on a second.

159
00:08:23,976 --> 00:08:24,976
Hey!

160
00:08:24,976 --> 00:08:25,976
Adachi!

161
00:08:25,976 --> 00:08:26,976
Huh?

162
00:08:26,976 --> 00:08:27,976
You got waxed on you, yeah?

163
00:08:27,976 --> 00:08:28,976
Give it here.

164
00:08:28,976 --> 00:08:29,976
You robbing the poor guy?

165
00:08:29,976 --> 00:08:31,976
Uh, uh, uh...

166
00:08:31,976 --> 00:08:34,976
I think that should do it.

167
00:08:34,976 --> 00:08:36,976
Serena wants to be a hair stylist one day.

168
00:08:36,976 --> 00:08:37,976
What?

169
00:08:37,976 --> 00:08:38,976
I never said that.

170
00:08:38,976 --> 00:08:40,976
It's just one option to look at.

171
00:08:40,976 --> 00:08:41,976
Geez.

172
00:08:41,976 --> 00:08:44,976
You do have really nice hair, though.

173
00:08:44,976 --> 00:08:47,976
Might be able to...

174
00:08:47,976 --> 00:08:48,976
There!

175
00:08:48,976 --> 00:08:49,976
How's that?

176
00:08:49,976 --> 00:08:50,976
Hm?

177
00:08:50,976 --> 00:08:51,976
It's like he's a thug!

178
00:08:51,976 --> 00:08:53,976
No one will give you crap now.

179
00:08:57,976 --> 00:08:58,976
Yamada?

180
00:08:58,976 --> 00:08:59,976
Don't worry.

181
00:08:59,976 --> 00:09:01,976
I am a model, after all.

182
00:09:01,976 --> 00:09:08,976
Just six months ago, I never could have imagined this situation.

183
00:09:08,976 --> 00:09:09,976
Enough of that.

184
00:09:09,976 --> 00:09:10,976
It's ribbon time.

185
00:09:10,976 --> 00:09:11,976
Oh, I forgot.

186
00:09:11,976 --> 00:09:12,976
But, uh...

187
00:09:12,976 --> 00:09:13,976
Hm?

188
00:09:13,976 --> 00:09:16,976
What's your deal, Bayashiko?

189
00:09:16,976 --> 00:09:17,976
Hm...

190
00:09:23,976 --> 00:09:24,976
Nothing.

191
00:09:24,976 --> 00:09:27,976
Just thinking how it's all over already.

192
00:09:27,976 --> 00:09:28,976
Huh?

193
00:09:28,976 --> 00:09:32,976
We'll be changing classes once we start year three.

194
00:09:33,976 --> 00:09:34,976
Hm.

195
00:09:34,976 --> 00:09:35,976
Yeah.

196
00:09:35,976 --> 00:09:37,976
They say they split up groups of troublemakers.

197
00:09:38,976 --> 00:09:39,976
So you think we're troublemakers?

198
00:09:40,976 --> 00:09:41,976
Well, we walk a fine line.

199
00:09:48,976 --> 00:09:50,976
We might end up in separate classes.

200
00:09:52,976 --> 00:09:53,976
We'll be fine.

201
00:09:54,976 --> 00:09:55,976
You know that?

202
00:09:55,976 --> 00:09:56,976
Not exactly.

203
00:09:56,976 --> 00:09:58,976
I don't...

204
00:09:58,976 --> 00:09:59,976
I don't...

205
00:09:59,976 --> 00:10:00,976
But...

206
00:10:01,976 --> 00:10:03,976
It doesn't hurt to believe it anyway.

207
00:10:08,976 --> 00:10:09,976
We're getting started!

208
00:10:09,976 --> 00:10:10,976
Line up in the hall.

209
00:10:10,976 --> 00:10:11,976
Uh...

210
00:10:14,976 --> 00:10:15,976
Wait a sec!

211
00:10:15,976 --> 00:10:17,976
You look the same as always!

212
00:10:19,976 --> 00:10:21,976
Thank you, Yoshida.

213
00:10:21,976 --> 00:10:22,976
Huh?

214
00:10:22,976 --> 00:10:23,976
Nah, no worries.

215
00:10:23,976 --> 00:10:24,976
Let's get going.

216
00:10:24,976 --> 00:10:27,976
Such a pain in the butt.

217
00:10:27,976 --> 00:10:28,976
Those chairs are too.

218
00:10:29,976 --> 00:10:30,976
Now then.

219
00:10:30,976 --> 00:10:32,976
Just gotta make sure I have my script.

220
00:10:34,976 --> 00:10:35,976
Huh?

221
00:10:36,976 --> 00:10:37,976
No!

222
00:10:40,976 --> 00:10:41,976
What?!

223
00:10:41,976 --> 00:10:42,976
You forgot your farewell speech?!

224
00:10:43,976 --> 00:10:44,976
But...

225
00:10:44,976 --> 00:10:45,976
Isn't it about to start?

226
00:10:46,976 --> 00:10:47,976
Relax, don't worry.

227
00:10:47,976 --> 00:10:48,976
I've gotcha!

228
00:10:48,976 --> 00:10:51,976
I'll find it and get it over to you as fast as I can!

229
00:10:52,976 --> 00:10:53,976
It's somewhere on your desk?

230
00:10:53,976 --> 00:10:54,976
Wait!

231
00:10:54,976 --> 00:10:56,976
I'm not gonna find any pervy stuff, am I?

232
00:10:56,976 --> 00:10:57,976
Just hurry!

233
00:10:58,976 --> 00:10:59,976
What do I do?

234
00:10:59,976 --> 00:11:01,976
Do I tell the teachers I can't do it?

235
00:11:01,976 --> 00:11:04,976
Just stop after the opening bit I do remember?

236
00:11:04,976 --> 00:11:05,976
Or should I...

237
00:11:06,976 --> 00:11:07,976
What's going on?

238
00:11:07,976 --> 00:11:08,976
Oh, uh...

239
00:11:10,976 --> 00:11:11,976
Actually...

240
00:11:12,976 --> 00:11:13,976
I'll do it!

241
00:11:13,976 --> 00:11:14,976
The address!

242
00:11:17,976 --> 00:11:18,976
It's nothing.

243
00:11:26,976 --> 00:11:27,976
Ichikawa?

244
00:11:28,976 --> 00:11:29,976
Please...

245
00:11:30,976 --> 00:11:31,976
Don't tell me I can do this!

246
00:11:32,976 --> 00:11:33,976
Don't say it!

247
00:11:34,976 --> 00:11:35,976
You can do this!

248
00:11:39,976 --> 00:11:40,976
Ta-da!

249
00:11:41,976 --> 00:11:42,976
That's...

250
00:11:42,976 --> 00:11:43,976
It's mine.

251
00:11:43,976 --> 00:11:44,976
But you hang on to it.

252
00:11:44,976 --> 00:11:45,976
Now let's go!

253
00:11:48,976 --> 00:11:49,976
Now let's go!

254
00:12:01,976 --> 00:12:02,976
Come on, I gotta make it!

255
00:12:02,976 --> 00:12:03,976
Hurry up!

256
00:12:04,976 --> 00:12:05,976
Come on!

257
00:12:06,976 --> 00:12:07,976
Hold on.

258
00:12:07,976 --> 00:12:09,976
Was his school this way or that way?

259
00:12:10,976 --> 00:12:11,976
Okay, what's the matter?

260
00:12:11,976 --> 00:12:12,976
Oh!

261
00:12:12,976 --> 00:12:13,976
Hey there, newbie!

262
00:12:13,976 --> 00:12:15,976
Do you happen to know the way to Daijuni Junior High?

263
00:12:16,976 --> 00:12:17,976
I used to go there.

264
00:12:18,976 --> 00:12:19,976
Thank goodness!

265
00:12:19,976 --> 00:12:21,976
Then can you show me the way there?

266
00:12:21,976 --> 00:12:22,976
Fine, keep up!

267
00:12:23,976 --> 00:12:24,976
Coming!

268
00:12:27,976 --> 00:12:32,976
Now then, next I would like to offer a congratulatory address to all those here today.

269
00:12:33,976 --> 00:12:34,976
There's no way I can do this!

270
00:12:35,976 --> 00:12:36,976
A speech with no script?

271
00:12:41,976 --> 00:12:42,976
At this rate...

272
00:12:43,976 --> 00:12:44,976
No!

273
00:12:44,976 --> 00:12:45,976
No!

274
00:12:45,976 --> 00:12:46,976
My arm!

275
00:12:46,976 --> 00:12:47,976
